# Java And Spring Rules

- Follow existing package boundaries under `ru.javazen.telegram.bot`.
- Keep controller logic light; move business logic to service classes.
- Reuse existing repository and model patterns for persistence updates.
- For config changes, prefer `application.yml` and existing config classes over ad-hoc constants.

# Change Discipline

- Preserve public behavior unless task explicitly requests behavioral change.
- Keep method signatures stable when used by XML wiring or interfaces.
- When adding new component beans, verify profile scope and startup impact.
